Planet Pipeline — Context File (TXT)

High-Level Architecture
- Inputs: radius, water_height, temp, moisture, altitude_bias, biome_scale, seed.
- Global Biome ID Map (GBM): cube/octa projection, one byte per texel.
- Virtual Texture (VT): albedo, normal, material layers streamed by page.
- Decal System: base author decals + runtime gameplay stamps.
- Navigation uses the same cube basis (sector grid + lazy flow/cost fields).
- Deformation updates mesh + VT overlay pages only where touched.

Invariants
- All LODs see the same biome id at the same surface coordinate.
- GBM is authoritative; VT is only the material realization.
- Cube/octa projection is shared across render, nav, decals, deformation.
- VT base pages are static; gameplay writes go to overlay deltas.
- Nav fields are lazy and disposable.

Coordinate System
- Surface point P = normalized direction * (radius + height).
- Basis mapping: normalize(P) → (face, u, v) via cube/octa projection.
- All subsystems must use the same basis library.

Data Models

1) Global Biome Map (GBM): R8
Cube faces:
  px.r8, nx.r8, py.r8, ny.r8, pz.r8, nz.r8
Metadata lists biome ids and names.

2) Virtual Texture (VT)
Page size: 128–256 px
Mips: several clip levels (orbit → ground)
Layers:
  albedo: BC7
  normal: BC5
  material: BC1/BC4 or custom param packing
Cache budget: a few thousand resident pages total.

3) Decal Records
Fields: id, blend mode, radius_m, albedo tint, roughness add, normal scale.
Author decals baked offline; gameplay decals stamped to overlay pages.

4) Navigation
Sector grid defined in the same cube projection.
Movement classes: land_small, land_heavy, hover, ship, submarine, seabed, air, orbital.
Fields per sector/class:
  cost: R8
  integration: R16 or R32F temp
  flow: packed direction (4-bit)

Build Pipeline

1) Climate Synthesis
- Compute temp/moisture/altitude fields.
- Classify to biome_id per texel.
- Output GBM faces.

2) VT Bake (Offline)
- For every page: evaluate biome material stacks + macro/noise.
- Compress pages.
- Apply author decals.
- Generate multi-mip clipmaps.

3) Packaging
- Group pages by mip ring or face.
- Store manifest with page hashes and offsets.

Runtime Streaming
- Frustum + horizon determine needed pages.
- Resolve (face, mip, page_u, page_v).
- Cache: LRU with prefetch in camera motion direction.
- Upload pages to GPU incrementally; avoid stalls.

Rendering
- Lookup biome_id via GBM.
- Sample VT (albedo/normal/material).
- Deferred lighting for sun + many point lights.
- Radial ambient for night-side readability.
- Forward pass only for transparent materials.
- Geometry LOD affects mesh density; material stays continuous.

Decals (Runtime)
- Stamp operations target overlay pages.
- Overlay blended in shader over base VT.
- Limit number of overlay pages; evict least-recent.

Deformation
- Apply CSG brush to surface mesh.
- Identify intersecting VT pages.
- Update overlay pages for crater/wear effects.
- Recompute local water fill.

Navigation
- A* on sector graph to choose corridor.
- Build cost/integration/flow only for needed sectors.
- Dynamic cost insertion for obstacles and congestion.
- Evict inactive sectors to keep memory bounded.

Performance Targets
- VT resident pages: ~3–6k
- Upload bandwidth: ~300–600 MB/s
- Deferred lighting with many small point lights
- Active nav sectors per class: bounded (~≤2000)

Failures / Guards
- Page thrash → increase prefetch/horizon.
- Seam mismatch → single shared basis math code.
- Excess overlay stamps → batch and merge writes.
- Deformation stall → run edits on worker threads.

Minimal Interfaces (Pseudocode)
biome_id_at(dir3) → u8
vt_sample(dir3, mip_bias) → {albedo, normal_ts, material}
vt_request_pages(range)
decal_stamp(def, center_dir3, radius_m, rotation)
deform_sphere(center_dir3, radius_m, depth_m, hardness)
build_flow(goal, move_class) → handle
query_dir(handle, dir3) → 2D direction
inject_cost(area, move_class, cost, ttl_ms)

Asset Formats
- GBM faces: raw R8 + JSON meta.
- VT pages: BCn compressed + manifest.
- Overlay pages: RGBA8/BCn depending on blend path.

Tooling Commands (Conceptual)
bake_gbm(...)
bake_vt(...)
bake_decals(...)
validate_basis(...)
profile_vt_cache(...)

Implementation Order
1) Basis mapping library
2) GBM generator and sampling
3) VT cache + shader sampling
4) Author and runtime decals
5) Deferred lighting + radial ambient
6) Nav sector + flow fields
7) Deformation with VT overlay updates

Acceptance Criteria
- Biome identity is stable across LOD.
- No visible tiling; decals provide breakup.
- LOD transitions are smooth; only detail refines.
- VT cache remains within memory limits.
- Deformations update shading and nav locally without stutter.
